{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1384886-god-machine-only-mostly-chronicle","id":1384886,"title":"God Machine Only (Mostly) Chronicle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-30T12:05:03-07:00","id":1384886,"title":"God Machine Only (Mostly) Chronicle","content":"The God Machine is one of my favorite horror setting ideas. Since the original core book came out, many splats have their own mythologies separate from the God Machine (e.g., Mage Supernal Realms).<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of running a chronicle or two where the God Machine is the default mythology. Other splat's mythologies aren't wholly true. Mages? They're actually aware enough about the machine's programming rules to tinker with it. Vampires, rogue remnants of a prior now shut down reality from Eastern Europe. <br /> <br /> Has anyone ever though of or done anything like this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T18:29:37-07:00","id":1385163,"title":"","content":"The GM is vast enough to be the one and only thing hiding in the shadows of the shadows.<br /> I wanted to move a recent chronicle in that direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus","name":"Mateus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24020_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-01T19:41:47-07:00","id":1385176,"title":"","content":"Something <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1342852-origins-of-theban-sorcery?p=1346540#post1346540\">Rose has mentioned</a> that makes it really easy to treat the God-Machine as the foundational mythology of the setting is that the Machine's basic canvas and toolbox is <i>structure itself</i> \u2014 any form of organization or pattern may have the Machine's DNA in it somewhere, even if its modern incarnation has prioritized things such that it no longer has direct input on the workings of other monsters without deliberate reclamation efforts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T16:10:31-07:00","id":1385317,"title":"","content":"Perfect thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}